-- BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-2 (2026-10-26, pillar autonomy; agent_issues 1000397 BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-1 and 1000266 BREACH-DOCTOR-1; ANTIFRAGILE-1: a single executor on a critical path ships with its second path).
-- Companion of qnfo-fleet-control 0.55.0 (POST /breach-doctor/run, qnfo-fleet-control/breach-doctor-run.test.mjs) and qnfo-cloud-ops 1.40.0 (jobBreachDoctorWatch calls it through the new FLEET_CONTROL
-- service binding when the doctor tick stalls, and drills it once a day, qnfo-cloud-ops/breach-doctor-watch-act.test.mjs).
-- State read 2026-10-26T12:32Z (SELECT only): agent_issues 1000397 open, high, its active contract issue-1000397 reads control_registry breach-doctor-switch alternate_tested_at and capability_ledger
-- breach-doctor:second-path-playbooks and fails (observed: no drill has read an alternate that acts when the doctor tick stops); control_registry breach-doctor-switch has alternate_tested_at NULL and an
-- alternate_path that says the watch "runs no playbook yet"; spof_registry "breach doctor tick (qnfo-fleet-control */10)" has alternate_tested_at NULL and an alternate_path that says the acting half stays open;
-- capability_ledger holds breach-doctor:second-path-watch (detect and report) and no second-path-playbooks row; the doctor ticks on the */10 slot (newest breach_diagnosis_events tick 12:20:50Z, mode=on);
-- failure_modes holds breach-doctor-watch-silent (the detect half) and nothing about the acting half.
-- What this file does (INSERT OR IGNORE and guarded UPDATE only, nothing deleted, alternate_tested_at NEVER written: the drill of jobBreachDoctorWatch stamps it, and only after a new tick row with source=watch exists):
--   * capability_ledger: breach-doctor:second-path-playbooks (provenance, prerequisites, reliability "unmeasured until the first drill"). This row is half of the closing probe of agent_issues 1000397.
--   * control_registry breach-doctor-switch: alternate_path names the acting half instead of "runs no playbook yet" (guarded REPLACE of that clause), evidence says why. spof_registry, doctor tick row: the same correction of the clause that said the acting half stays open.
--   * agent_issues 1000397: one paragraph says what was delivered; the issue stays OPEN and closes through its own probe once the first drill has stamped the alternate. Its contract's precondition and action text
--     stop saying the playbook branch is unbuilt; the probe is untouched.
--   * failure mode breach-doctor-second-path-undrilled with its fm- detector contract: the acting half has not verified a run for 1560 minutes (the 1440-minute drill plus the 120 minutes SLA-120M-1 allows a
--     freshness check on a loop slower than 120 minutes) while the doctor is not off, so a broken binding, a 403 or a route that errors cannot stay silent behind a declared alternate.
--   * one decision_log row.
-- spof-review: one service binding from qnfo-cloud-ops to qnfo-fleet-control (props.caller qnfo-cloud-ops, no key), no new worker, cron or table. Net-zero: the second path replaces nothing and adds no loop, it
-- gives the existing watch job a call. The fleet graph (impact of worker:qnfo-fleet-control) lists the dashboard and qnfo-ops as binders already; this adds qnfo-cloud-ops.
-- charter-pillar: autonomy.
-- APPLY-BY: ci
-- DB: qnfo-audit
-- Rollback: DELETE FROM remediation_contracts WHERE class = 'fm-breach-doctor-second-path-undrilled'; DELETE FROM failure_modes WHERE fm_key = 'breach-doctor-second-path-undrilled'; DELETE FROM capability_ledger WHERE capability = 'breach-doctor:second-path-playbooks'; UPDATE control_registry SET alternate_path = replace(alternate_path, 'qnfo-cloud-ops jobBreachDoctorWatch (BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-1 1.39.0 detects, BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-2 1.40.0 acts) reads the same switch and writes nothing while it is off, and when the newest doctor tick is older than 30 minutes (and once a day as a drill) calls POST /breach-doctor/run on qnfo-fleet-control through the FLEET_CONTROL service binding, which runs the same breachDoctorTick with the same validators, a drill stamps alternate_tested_at only after a new breach_diagnosis_events tick row with source=watch exists', 'qnfo-cloud-ops jobBreachDoctorWatch (BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-1, 1.39.0, built) reads the same switch and writes nothing while it is off, but runs no playbook yet, so this alternate stays untested until the acting half of issue BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-1 lands'), evidence = replace(evidence, ' | BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-2 2026-10-26: alternate_path now names the acting half (FLEET_CONTROL service binding, POST /breach-doctor/run), alternate_tested_at is still written by the drill alone', '') WHERE control = 'breach-doctor-switch'; UPDATE spof_registry SET alternate_path = replace(alternate_path, 'It makes no model call. BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-2 (qnfo-cloud-ops 1.40.0, qnfo-fleet-control 0.55.0): when the age passes 30 minutes it also calls POST /breach-doctor/run on qnfo-fleet-control through the FLEET_CONTROL service binding (at most once in 30 minutes), which runs the same breachDoctorTick in its own invocation, so a starved or crashed */10 slot no longer stops the diagnosis path, and a daily drill does the same while the doctor is healthy.', 'It makes no model call and runs no playbook: it notices and reports the stall, the diagnosis path itself keeps one runner, and the acting half (running the validated per-issue playbooks when the tick is stale) stays open as issue BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-1.'), evidence = replace(evidence, ' | BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-2 2026-10-26 (agent_issues 1000397): alternate_path now names the acting half, alternate_tested_at is stamped by the daily drill of jobBreachDoctorWatch only after a new tick row with source=watch exists, and by the chaos drill probe of this component', '') WHERE component = 'breach doctor tick (qnfo-fleet-control */10)'; UPDATE agent_issues SET description = substr(description, 1, instr(description, char(10) || char(10) || 'BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-2 2026-10-26 (qnfo-fleet-control 0.55.0') - 1) WHERE id = (SELECT id FROM agent_issues WHERE title LIKE 'BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-1:%' ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT 1) AND instr(description, 'BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-2 2026-10-26 (qnfo-fleet-control 0.55.0') > 0; UPDATE remediation_contracts SET precondition = 'BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-1 (qnfo-cloud-ops 1.39.0) detects, measures and reports a stalled doctor tick but runs no playbook, so the diagnosis path still has one runner', action = 'a session adds the playbook branch to jobBreachDoctorWatch in qnfo-cloud-ops (the detect and report half is deployed) and the control_alternate_probes row for breach-doctor-switch, the stale-PR lane merges it and the canonical deploy ships it' WHERE class = 'issue-' || (SELECT id FROM agent_issues WHERE title LIKE 'BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-1:%' ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT 1) AND instr(precondition, 'BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-2') > 0;
-- Rollback note: the decision_log row stays (append-only), an alternate_tested_at or last_exercised_at a verified drill stamped stays (it was earned), the cloud_ops_events run rows stay, and the worker changes revert with the canonical deploy canary.

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO capability_ledger (capability, provenance, prerequisites, reliability, acquired_at, last_exercised_at, evidence) VALUES
 ('breach-doctor:second-path-playbooks',
  'BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-2 (qnfo-fleet-control 0.55.0 POST /breach-doctor/run, qnfo-cloud-ops 1.40.0 jobBreachDoctorWatch, migrations/2026-10-26-breach-doctor-watch3-acting.sql)',
  'qnfo-cloud-ops FLEET_CONTROL service binding with props.caller qnfo-cloud-ops (installed by qnfo-ops BINDING-PROPS-APPLY-1 on the canonical deploy), qnfo-fleet-control 0.55.0 live, breach_diagnosis_events, ops_config breach_doctor not off',
  'unmeasured until the first drill: a cloud_ops_events run row (id breach-doctor-watch-run-*) with status ok and a breach_diagnosis_events tick row with source=watch whose tick_id the route returned',
  strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now'), NULL,
  'when the doctor tick is older than 30 minutes the fleet runs the breach doctor from a second worker through a service binding, and once a day proves that path while the doctor is healthy, without a session and without a copy of the validators');

UPDATE control_registry SET alternate_path = replace(alternate_path, 'qnfo-cloud-ops jobBreachDoctorWatch (BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-1, 1.39.0, built) reads the same switch and writes nothing while it is off, but runs no playbook yet, so this alternate stays untested until the acting half of issue BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-1 lands',
    'qnfo-cloud-ops jobBreachDoctorWatch (BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-1 1.39.0 detects, BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-2 1.40.0 acts) reads the same switch and writes nothing while it is off, and when the newest doctor tick is older than 30 minutes (and once a day as a drill) calls POST /breach-doctor/run on qnfo-fleet-control through the FLEET_CONTROL service binding, which runs the same breachDoctorTick with the same validators, a drill stamps alternate_tested_at only after a new breach_diagnosis_events tick row with source=watch exists'),
  evidence = evidence || ' | BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-2 2026-10-26: alternate_path now names the acting half (FLEET_CONTROL service binding, POST /breach-doctor/run), alternate_tested_at is still written by the drill alone'
WHERE control = 'breach-doctor-switch'
  AND instr(alternate_path, 'qnfo-cloud-ops jobBreachDoctorWatch (BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-1, 1.39.0, built) reads the same switch and writes nothing while it is off, but runs no playbook yet, so this alternate stays untested until the acting half of issue BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-1 lands') > 0;

UPDATE spof_registry SET alternate_path = replace(alternate_path, 'It makes no model call and runs no playbook: it notices and reports the stall, the diagnosis path itself keeps one runner, and the acting half (running the validated per-issue playbooks when the tick is stale) stays open as issue BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-1.',
    'It makes no model call. BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-2 (qnfo-cloud-ops 1.40.0, qnfo-fleet-control 0.55.0): when the age passes 30 minutes it also calls POST /breach-doctor/run on qnfo-fleet-control through the FLEET_CONTROL service binding (at most once in 30 minutes), which runs the same breachDoctorTick in its own invocation, so a starved or crashed */10 slot no longer stops the diagnosis path, and a daily drill does the same while the doctor is healthy.'),
  evidence = evidence || ' | BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-2 2026-10-26 (agent_issues 1000397): alternate_path now names the acting half, alternate_tested_at is stamped by the daily drill of jobBreachDoctorWatch only after a new tick row with source=watch exists, and by the chaos drill probe of this component'
WHERE component = 'breach doctor tick (qnfo-fleet-control */10)'
  AND instr(alternate_path, 'It makes no model call and runs no playbook: it notices and reports the stall, the diagnosis path itself keeps one runner, and the acting half (running the validated per-issue playbooks when the tick is stale) stays open as issue BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-1.') > 0;

UPDATE agent_issues SET description = description || char(10) || char(10) || 'BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-2 2026-10-26 (qnfo-fleet-control 0.55.0, qnfo-cloud-ops 1.40.0, migrations/2026-10-26-breach-doctor-watch3-acting.sql). DELIVERED: the acting half. When doctor_tick_age_min is above 30 and ops_config breach_doctor is not off, jobBreachDoctorWatch calls POST /breach-doctor/run on qnfo-fleet-control through the FLEET_CONTROL service binding (props.caller qnfo-cloud-ops, at most once in 30 minutes). The route runs the same breachDoctorTick, so the same validators, loop_lock and live-case index, in its own invocation, and the tick writes its breach_diagnosis_events row with source=watch. Nothing of the engine is copied into qnfo-cloud-ops. A drill does the same once a day while the doctor is healthy. Only a run whose tick row exists stamps control_registry breach-doctor-switch and spof_registry alternate_tested_at and capability_ledger last_exercised_at. This issue stays open until that first drill and closes by its own probe: the capability row exists from this migration and alternate_tested_at is written by the drill alone.'
WHERE id = (SELECT id FROM agent_issues WHERE title LIKE 'BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-1:%' ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT 1)
  AND status = 'open' AND instr(description, 'BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-2 2026-10-26 (qnfo-fleet-control 0.55.0') = 0;

UPDATE remediation_contracts SET precondition = 'BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-2 (qnfo-fleet-control 0.55.0, qnfo-cloud-ops 1.40.0) runs the doctor from qnfo-cloud-ops when the tick stalls, the first drill has not stamped control_registry breach-doctor-switch yet',
  action = 'jobBreachDoctorWatch runs the first drill on its next tick after the qnfo-cloud-ops 1.40.0 and qnfo-fleet-control 0.55.0 deploys and stamps the alternate once a new tick row with source=watch exists, the hourly remediation tick then runs this probe and closes the issue'
WHERE class = 'issue-' || (SELECT id FROM agent_issues WHERE title LIKE 'BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-1:%' ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT 1)
  AND instr(precondition, 'runs no playbook') > 0
  AND (SELECT status FROM agent_issues WHERE title LIKE 'BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-1:%' ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT 1) = 'open';

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO failure_modes (fm_key, failure_mode, root_cause, remediation, detector, probe_class, first_seen, issue_id, trigger_condition, symptom, blast_radius)
VALUES ('breach-doctor-second-path-undrilled', 'the acting half of the breach doctor second path has not verified a run for longer than its daily drill plus 120 minutes, so the alternate is declared and untested',
  'qnfo-cloud-ops jobBreachDoctorWatch calls POST /breach-doctor/run on qnfo-fleet-control through the FLEET_CONTROL service binding: a missing binding (a deploy that landed before it), a binding without props.caller (HTTP 403), a lock that never frees, a route that errors or a tick that writes no source=watch row each end the run with an error code in its run row, and nothing else reads the run rows',
  'fm-breach-doctor-second-path-undrilled reads capability_ledger breach-doctor:second-path-playbooks, whose last_exercised_at only a verified run writes: 1560 minutes (the 1440-minute drill plus the 120 minutes SLA-120M-1 allows) without one is a failure, counted from the capability row when no run has verified yet. The run rows are cloud_ops_events kind breach-doctor-watch, ids breach-doctor-watch-run-*, and carry the error code',
  'fm-breach-doctor-second-path-undrilled: the doctor ledger exists, breach_doctor is not off, and the newest verified run of the second path (capability_ledger last_exercised_at) is at most 1560 minutes old',
  'fm-breach-doctor-second-path-undrilled', strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now'), 1000397,
  'breach_diagnosis_events exists, ops_config breach_doctor is not off, and breach-doctor:second-path-playbooks has neither last_exercised_at nor an acquired_at within 1560 minutes',
  'the second path of the breach doctor is declared in control_registry and spof_registry but no run of it has been seen by a tick row with source=watch',
  'the second path of the breach doctor (the first path is unaffected)');

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO remediation_contracts (class, issue_id, precondition, action, verify_probe, verify_transport, max_attempts, escalate_to, expected_cadence_h, status, module, next_due_at)
VALUES ('fm-breach-doctor-second-path-undrilled', NULL, 'BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-2', 'failure-mode detector',
  'SELECT ''0'' AS expected, CASE WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM sqlite_master WHERE type = ''table'' AND name = ''breach_diagnosis_events'') AND lower(trim(COALESCE((SELECT value FROM ops_config WHERE key = ''breach_doctor''), ''''))) NOT IN (''off'', ''0'', ''false'', ''no'', ''disabled'') AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM capability_ledger WHERE capability = ''breach-doctor:second-path-playbooks'' AND COALESCE(last_exercised_at, acquired_at) < strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'', ''now'', ''-1560 minutes'')) THEN ''1'' ELSE ''0'' END AS observed',
  'd1-query', 3, 'qnfo-fleet-control', 1, 'active', 'failure-mode', datetime('now'));

INSERT INTO decision_log (actor, assumption, action, evidence, outcome, blast_radius, rollback_path, capability_gain, predicted_outcome, reach_gain, surfaces_tested)
SELECT 'session_01QpQv19uh1padRwZ3u1r766',
  'a second path that only reports a stall is not a second path (ANTIFRAGILE-1), the observed failure class is a starved or crashed */10 slot of qnfo-fleet-control and not a dead D1, the second runner must RUN the engine and not copy its validators (the validator was patched three times in one day: 0.53.0, 0.53.1, 0.53.2), a Worker cannot fetch a workers.dev host of its own account (issue 1190) so the call must be a service binding with props.caller, and an alternate counts only after a drill has seen it run',
  'BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-2: qnfo-fleet-control 0.55.0 POST /breach-doctor/run (answers only a service binding whose props.caller is qnfo-cloud-ops, 403 and no write otherwise, 409 while breach_doctor is off) runs breachDoctorTick once in its own invocation and records its tick event with source=watch. qnfo-cloud-ops 1.40.0 jobBreachDoctorWatch calls it through the new FLEET_CONTROL binding when doctor_tick_age_min is above 30 (at most once in 30 minutes, claimed by a run row before the call) and once a day as a drill, and stamps control_registry breach-doctor-switch, spof_registry (doctor tick) and capability_ledger breach-doctor:second-path-playbooks only after a new tick row with source=watch and the route''s tick_id exists. The write-ahead of the sql and file-issue actions is now a compare-and-set on state = diagnosed, so two ticks that both hold a lock cannot act on one case twice',
  'qnfo-audit 2026-10-26T12:32Z (SELECT only): agent_issues 1000397 open, its contract issue-1000397 last_verdict fail; control_registry breach-doctor-switch alternate_tested_at NULL with the text "runs no playbook yet"; spof_registry doctor tick alternate_tested_at NULL; capability_ledger has breach-doctor:second-path-watch and no second-path-playbooks; breach_diagnosis_events ticks every 10 minutes (newest 12:20:50Z, mode=on, err=none); the offline suites ran the real route and the real job on node:sqlite over fixtures with the live column lists, including a cron tick and a watch tick at once and a tick that lost its lock',
  'migration applied by CI at merge, the qnfo-fleet-control 0.55.0 and qnfo-cloud-ops 1.40.0 deploys follow with their canaries: proof to read later is a cloud_ops_events row id breach-doctor-watch-run-d-* with status ok, a breach_diagnosis_events tick row with source=watch and the same tick_id, control_registry breach-doctor-switch alternate_tested_at set, and agent_issues 1000397 closed by its probe',
  'one capability_ledger row, one failure mode with its detector contract, text corrections on two registry rows, one paragraph on one issue and one contract text; the route runs the same engine the */10 slot runs, under the same lock, switch and caps, and refuses every caller but qnfo-cloud-ops; the job writes cloud_ops_events run rows (at most one per 30 minutes while stalled, one a day otherwise) and, after a verified run, three stamps in one batch',
  'the Rollback header of migrations/2026-10-26-breach-doctor-watch3-acting.sql restores the texts and removes the rows this file created; the workers revert with the canonical deploy canary, and removing the FLEET_CONTROL binding makes the job report skipped no-binding',
  'the breach doctor runs from a second worker when the */10 slot of qnfo-fleet-control is starved or crashes, and the second path is proven once a day, without a session',
  'within 30 minutes of the qnfo-cloud-ops 1.40.0 deploy a run row breach-doctor-watch-run-d-* has status ok (the first drill runs on the first tick after the deploy) and issue 1000397 closes on its probe within the next 60 minutes',
  'none',
  'd1:qnfo-audit read-only, node:sqlite fixtures in qnfo-fleet-control/breach-doctor-run.test.mjs, qnfo-cloud-ops/breach-doctor-watch-act.test.mjs and migrations/breach-doctor-watch-acting.test.mjs'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM decision_log WHERE action LIKE 'BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-2:%');
